Z||000000||BAM-BAM||06-17-2000||10:07 PM||||  What did they use to keep the rear decklid up on the notchbacks with spoilers? I just put a spoiler on my 85GT and now the decklid won't stay up. I know that there must be something other than the hinged springs, right? If not then I need to know what to use. TIA for any and all advice.<P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||06-17-2000||10:21 PM||||The torsion arms are different. One set has a yellow dot and one set has a red dot. Check the color you have and get the other to handle the weight of the wing.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||06-17-2000||10:26 PM||||I just used a broom handle to prop the lid up on my 85 SE. The ironic thing is my T-top car has no spoiler but the springs are set for one. The girl I bought the car from had her keys on the lid and when she pushed the button to open the hatch, it threw the keys about 15 feet down the road! I laughed, she did not. I wonder why?||||reg||1
Z||000003||ka4nkf||06-17-2000||10:27 PM||||The best way is to install a strut. check with rodney dickman he has the strut kit very reasonable.||||reg||1
Z||000004||SCCA FIERO||06-17-2000||11:45 PM||||There are 3 different positions that you can set the tension for the lid. If you look near the hinges you can see the holes. If yours is set to the middle one, take the pin out and move it to the rear one to give it a little more tension. This is easier said than done though. You have to pull the rods back to remove the pins, then pull even harder to pull the rods back far enough to insert the pin in the next hole. <P>Let us know how many fingers you break  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||BAM-BAM||06-18-2000||01:14 AM||||   This is why I love this Forum; just ask and ye shall recieve. Thanks for you inputs.<P> Orief: Thanks I'll check on the dot to make sure what I'm set for.<P> Cooter: C'mon now, I don't want to have to resort to the broom thing.<P> ka4nkf: If all else fails, that's exactly what I will do; thanks.<P> SCCA: I'll try that first thing after I look for the magic dot.<P> Thanks again, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
